Refactored StreamedKeyList components to use shared utilities

• Created `src/app/key/lib.ts` with shared utilities:
  - `KeyPair` interface for type consistency
  - `colorMap` constant for score-based color mapping
  - `getColorForScore()` function to determine color tier
  - `formatClipboardText()` function for consistent clipboard formatting
  - `useStreamedKeys()` hook that encapsulates all streaming logic and state management

• Updated `src/app/key/encryption/streamed-key-list.tsx`:
  - Removed duplicate streaming logic, state management, and color mapping
  - Now uses shared `useStreamedKeys` hook and `getColorForScore` function
  - Maintained encryption-specific unique key generation pattern
  - Reduced component from 158 lines to 48 lines

• Updated `src/app/key/signing/streamed-key-list.tsx`:
  - Removed duplicate streaming logic, state management, and color mapping
  - Now uses shared `useStreamedKeys` hook and `getColorForScore` function
  - Maintained signing-specific key generation pattern (simpler than encryption)
  - Reduced component from 158 lines to 46 lines

The refactoring eliminates ~200 lines of duplicate code while maintaining the same functionality and preserving the subtle differences between encryption and signing key display patterns.

Added signed-note page with cryptographic message signing and encryption

• Created `src/app/signed-note/page.tsx` - Server component for signed note functionality
  - Generates Ed25519 signing keys and X25519 encryption keys
  - Implements `processSignedNote` server action for cryptographic operations
  - Uses ECIES (Elliptic Curve Integrated Encryption Scheme) for message encryption
  - Displays generated key pairs in read-only form inputs
  - Includes informational "How it Works" section

• Created `src/components/SignedNoteForm.tsx` - Client component for form handling
  - Manages form submission state and loading indicators
  - Handles POST-based form submissions with FormData (no URL parameter limits)
  - Displays validation results with success/error badges
  - Shows original vs decrypted message comparison
  - Renders complete ECIES message format with parsed components
  - Dynamic textarea sizing based on content length
  - Proper error handling without page redirects

Key features implemented:
• Ed25519 digital signature generation and verification
• X25519 encryption using ephemeral keys
• ECIES message format with ephemeral public key, ciphertext, and signature
• Automatic message validation through decrypt-and-compare
• Component parsing showing IV, auth tag, raw ciphertext, and signature
• Server/client component separation following Next.js App Router patterns
• POST-based form submission supporting large messages
• Real-time form processing with loading states